tration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 15 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast and axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm axillary tail  and a REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm skin ellipse containing a 1 5cm nipple  A short stitch on the skin ellipse marks superior and a long stitch lateral  as designated by the surgeon  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a centrally located  ill defined fibrous area  approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  A distinct mass lesion is not identified  The remainder of the breast tissue consists of lobular adipose tissue with thin fibrous bands  The posterior margin appears grossly unremarkable throughout the specimen  The axillary tail contains multiple lymph nodes and soft tissue nodules measuring REMOVED_DATE to approximately 2 0cm in greatest dimension  many of these contain a waxy yellow homogeneous substance  Multiple matted lymph nodes nodules are present which cannot be individually dissected  Section code  A J  representative sections of fibrous area suspicious for tumor  K L  representative sections of posterior margin  central portion of specimen  M  representative section of skin  N Q  single lymph nodes nodules  R S  one bisected lymph node nodule each cassette  T Y  representative sections of matted lymph nodes nodules  Resident  ELENA BRACHTEL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Poor_(g