SULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 97 at 15 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 28 x 10 8cm ellipse of white skin containing a 2 7cm in diameter distorted nipple and areola  The surrounding 7 x 6cm skin is firm  darkened and contains a REMOVED_DATE x 1cm ulceration inferomedially and a 3 3cm linear indentation   scar   lateral to the nipple  The fibroadipose tissue deep to the skin measures 24 x 17 x 8 5cm and is contiguous with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm axillary tail  Deep to the firm area on the skin is an 8 x 7 x 5cm tan to white  firm  ill defined mass  Strands of tan tissue approach to within 0 5cm of the superior and inferior superficial soft tissue margins  Multiple REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm satellite nodules are present in the specimen and one 0 4cm tan nodule abuts the inferior deep inked margin  However  the medial and lateral resectiion margins are greater than 2cm from gross tumor  The axillary tail contains multiple lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm  All the lymph nodes are white and rubbery  Section Code A B   nipple and tumor C D   representative ulcer E F   firm skin adjacent to nipple G   scar H K   representative tumor L M   superior superficial margin  radial sections N   inferior superficial  radial margin O   medial  en face margin P   lateral  en face margin Q   deep radial margin R U   lymph nodes EE FF   deep margin  radial section GG   deep inferior margin  radial section Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are multiple parts  Labeled  superior margin left breast  is a tissue fragment  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  soft  yellow tan  submitted entirely as frozen  1 in V  Labeled  inferior margin left breast  is a fragment of soft  yellow tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  entirely frozen as frozen  2 and submitted in W  Labeled  new superior margin  is a 16cm long and 0 9cm wide skin ellipse excised to a depth of 1 4cm  A stitch designates the opposite surface to the new superior margin  The new margin is inked and representative  non stitch  margin is frozen as frozen  3  5  in X to Z respectively  Additional unfrozen new superior margin from the peripheral ends of the skin ellipse are submitted in AA and BB  Labeled  superior margin  3  left breast  and  suture on inferior margin  is a 7 x 0 9cm wide skin ellipse excised to a depth of 1 4cm with a suture in place on the inferior margin  The skin ellipse is unremarkable  Representative new superior margin is taken from the central portion of the ellipse and frozen as frozen  6 in CC  The remainder of this newest superior margin is e