Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Resident  Matthew M Johnson  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Andrew E Rosenberg  MD Frozen Section Consultant s   Melinda J Lerwill  M D  Frozen Section Resident  James E  Davis  M D  Signed Out by  Joshua Kish  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  2 2 CM  WITH ADENOSQUAMOUS AND SPINDLE FEATURES  FOCALLY POSITIVE AT A TISSUE MARGIN  2  HEALING BIOPSY SITE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  This is an unusual carcinoma that consists of a relatively well circumscribed nodule of malignant cells with focal squamous differentiation and malignant spindle cells with a moderate mitotic rate  Focally  the spindle cells merge with the carcinoma cells supporting a histologic relationship  Immunohistochemical stains for heavy chain myosin  calponin  p63  and cytokeratin highlight the lack of myoepithelial cells around many of the glands as well as single epithelial cells  Stains for cytokeratin 903  wide spectrum keratin  and epithelial membrane antigen also highlight the single cells  The case has been reviewed with Drs  Sgroi  Koerner  and Lerwill who agree with the above interpretation  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  BREAST  LEFT  MEDIAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  CEPHALAD FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  CAUDAD FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  LATERAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are five containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  final shaved margin medial   is an unoriented  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  final shaved margin cephalad   is an unoriented  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  final shaved margin caudad   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of unoriented tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  final shaved margin lateral   is an unoriented  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of unoriented tan yellow lobular shiny unremarkable appearing breast tissue  The external surface is inked black  Sectioning reveals a well circumscribed  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  firm  tan pink to gray mass  Representative sections are frozen as frozen section  1   1A and  1B  now resubmitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   respectively  No other lesions or masses are identified  The rest of the mass is submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  BREAST  LEFT  MASS   EXCISION  ATYPICAL GLANDULAR AND STROMAL PROLIFERATION  AWAIT FURTHER EVALUATION ON PERMANENTS  Final Diagnosis by Joshua Kish M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Rare tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT  MEDIAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  CEPHALAD FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT  