  McKee MD Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13 35 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left modified radical mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm breast  with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm of attached axillary tail and a suture designating 12 o clock  The surface REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm tan skin ellipse has an eccentric REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  raised  nipple areolar complex  Located 1 2cm lateral to the nipple is a 4 0cm well healed linear scar  The specimen is black inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm hemorrhagic cavity  contiguous with the overlying scar  coming to within 1 0cm of the deep and 2 1cm of the anterior margin  The remaining parenchyma is predominantly dense  white  fibrous tissue admixed with yellow  lobulated fatty tissue  Within the attached axilla are multiple tan red  rubbery to tan white  firm lymph nodes measuring from 0 3cm to 2 2cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE  A B  Cavity to deep margin  C E  Representative sections of cavity  F G  Fibrous tissue away from cavity  H L multiple lymph nodes  M   One bisected lymph node  N O  One bisected lymph node  Gross Description by  LORI MARINI Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  MASTECTOMY , Moderate_(grade_II).
