sterior margins of the specimen respectively  The remaining breast contains a moderate to marked amount of tan white rubbery fibrous tissue  No additional discrete masses or lesions are noted  The axillary region is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the central medial gritty area  with closest margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the central breast parenchyma between the two gritty areas   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the central lateral gritty area  with closest margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the upper outer breast quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the lower outer breast quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the lower inner breast quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the upper inner breast quadrant  Received in formalin  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast skin   are multiple fragments of unremarkable skin that aggregate to 3 x 2cm  excised to a depth of 0 5cm  The soft tissue margins are inked black and representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL NODES   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M D   Electronically signed on Thursday February 12   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 03 15PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progest