 fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm mastectomy specimen partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm skin ellipse with a centrally located 2 5cm in diameter nipple areolar complex  The specimen is oriented with a short stitch  superior  and a long stitch  lateral   A 1 5cm in diameter hemorrhagic defect is present at the inferior edge of the skin ellipse  1 5cm laterally from the nipple areolar complex  The specimen is inked blue anteriorly  black posteriorly and serially sectioned to reveal a 5 5cm in diameter  rounded cavity with hemorrhagic content and firm wall measuring up to 1 0cm in diameter and abutting the posterior resection margin  connecting to the anterior resection margin through the previously described defect  3 0cm away from the inferior resection margin  The remaining parenchyma is characterized by tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue intermixed with fibrous breast tissue  slightly nodular  rubbery and geographically confluent   No other firm areas are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  M N  cavity in relation to the posterior margins  O  cavity in relation to the anterior margin  P  cavity towards superior  Q  fibrosed area 3 5cm in maximum diameter adjacent to the blue tracing ink  superior edge   R  fibrous breast tissue at the lateral edge of the skin ellipse  Additional breast tissue is submitted in cassettes CC to LL  Resident  MASSIMO D APUZZO  MD PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS REMOVED_DATE  LYMPH NODES  LEFT SENTINEL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  TRACY L  DAVIS  MD   Ph D  O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  L