cavity is located within the mid to inferior aspect of the specimen and is located 0 6cm from the black inked posterior aspect and 1 5cm from the overlying scar bearing skin  The cavity lining is tan pink  focally hemorrhagic smooth and glistening  The cavity borders are indurated and grossly unremarkable  Located 4 0cm superior lateral is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm ill defined  tan white centrally hemorrhagic irregular area that comes to 1 5cm from the black inked posterior margin and 2 2cm from the anterior skin surface  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma consist of tan yellow pink  lobulated unremarkable fibroadipose tissue with no additional discrete masses or lesions identified  The most lateral and superior aspect at the posterior margin is a slightly indurated  REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm area displaying a smooth and glistening dark red to tan fibrotic surface rimmed by tan yellow tissue  Lymph nodes are not identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Closest extent of cavity to posterior margin  B  Closest extent of cavity to anterior skin margin with scar  C D  Representative sections of cavity wall  E  Separate lateral nodule to deep margin  F G  Uninvolved parenchyma  H I  Fibrotic smooth walled cavity at posterior aspect  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  FCK                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Moderate_(grade_II).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 27 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  ADDED INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS Revised by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Revised on 31 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 54                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   NEW SUPERIOR MARGIN    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 12 OF 12 NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Edited by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 24                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 06 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  with attached REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm unremarkable skin ellipse and stitches designating the margins with one stitch respresenting the superior margin  two stitches the medial margin  The specimen is inked in black overlaid with blue superiorly  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm stellate white tan firm tumor mass  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  the firm nodule approaches the superior resection margin and is 0 4cm from the inferior resection margin  0 4cm from the deep margin and 0 6cm from the medial margin and 1 5cm from the lateral margin  Frozen section is resubmitted in cassette A  Two closest resection margins  Superior  submitted in B and C  Tumor with deep margins submitted in D  A representative section of the main breast tissue submitted in E and F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue from which multiple tan pink lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 6cm are dissected away and submitted entirely in cassettes G through K  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  New superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue inked and sectioned to 