   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 06 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of breast tissue with a localizing wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fairly well circumscribed tan pink fleshy nodule coming to within 0 1cm of the inked surface  adjacent to the nodule is a more ill defined firm fibrous tissue  The nodule and surrounding tissue is submitted in cassettes A E  A representative section of the breast away from the nodule in cassette F  The remainder of the breast is grossly unremarkable  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  new reexcision superior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of breast tissue with true superior margin inked in blue  The tissue is inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes G J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of adipose tissue from which multiple lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  A representative section from each lymph node is submitted in cassettes L R  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   DISCRETE NODULE W