Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 50 CLINICAL DATA  59 year old female with core biopsy positive for carcinoma of the right breast  now undergoing right lumpectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MEASURED FROM SECTION C   GRADE 1 OF 3  WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE CLOSEST MARGINS  SUPERIOR AND INFERIOR   PRESENT ON THREE OF TEN SLIDES  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  SINGLE FOCUS ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE TUMOR  AWAY FROM MARGINS   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   REGIONAL DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  SINGLE FOCUS WITHIN THE SUBCAPSULAR SINUS OF ONE OF NINETEEN LYMPH NODES  LEVELS EXAMINED   Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 33                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone recptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive 