 U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 10 47 Consulting Pathologist s   Grace T  McKee MD GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel lymph node  is a 0 6cm in diameter lymph node  entirely frozen as FX  1  now in A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of breast tissue  The surgeon has oriented the specimen with 2 stitches furthest from the biopsy cavity  This surface is inked in black  Representative sections with the distant margin are submitted in B G  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibrofatty breast tissue  previously dyed blue  with a needle localization wire in place  The surgeon has oriented the specimen with the short stitch superior and the long stitch lateral  The anterior surface is inked black  the posterior surface is inked blue  with the superior edge over inked in orange  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm ill defined area of white yellow discoloration that is firm and rubbery  This area abuts the anterior inferior and posterior margins  and is 1 5cm away from the superior margin  Representative sections of the area of abnormality with closest margins are submitted in H K  Representative sections of areas away from the abnormality are submitted in L M  Resident  ALIYAH RAHEMTULLAH  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D     