eral  The deep margin is inked black  and the inferior margin is inked blue  The specimen is sequentially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan white  hemorrhagic  fibrotic area  within the lower outer quadrant of the specimen subjacent to the umbilicated portion of skin  This fibrotic area extends to the deep margin  No definite tumors are identified  The remainder of the cut surface is yellow white and unremarkable  A few potential lymph nodes are identified within the small portion of axillary tail  measuring up to 0 7cm  Representative sections are submitted as labeled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrotic area  with sections to deep margin in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and a section to the anterior margin and skin in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Random sections away from lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Six potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous tissue to deep  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous tissue to anterior Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast tissue with additional superficial lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of yellow pink irregular fragments of fibrofatty tissue  The cut surfaces are yellow white  with focal 0 2cm cyst filled with bloody serous fluid  No additional lesions are appreciated  Representative sections are submitted in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Michael R Tan  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Michael R Tan  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts Gen