istics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 15 02 Consulting Pathologist s   Grace T  McKee MD GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x 8 x 2 5cm lumpectomy specimen with attached two localization wires  The specimen is oriented by a short stitch designating anterior  a long stitch designating lateral  and a bow tie designating cephalad  The specimen is inked blue in the anterior aspect and black in the posterior aspect  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  relatively well circumscribed  tan white  slightly glistening mass which comes to 0 4cm from the posterior resection margin  0 8cm from the anterior resection margin  1 5cm from the lateral resection margin  and is away from the superior  inferior  and medial resection margins  Also identified 0 6cm inferior to the mass is a 0 2cm nodule  which comes to 0 6cm from the anterior resection margin  0 8cm from the posterior resection margin and 0 2cm from the inferior resection margin and is away from the other resection margins  The remaining breast parenchyma is fatty  SECTION CODE A  Mass with posterior resection margin B  Mass with anterior resection margin C  Mass with lateral resection margin D E  Additional sections of the mass F  Nodule with posterior resection margin G  Nodule with anterior resection margin H  Nodule with inferior resection margin Resident  Mari Mino  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_AC