Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 11 23 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  CARCINOSARCOMA WITH FOCAL CARTILAGINOUS AND OSSEOUS DIFFERENTIATION  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor is composed of both malignant epithelial and mesenchymal  sarcomatous  areas  These two components are distinct and do not show any merging from the carcinoma into the sarcoma  Immunoperoxidase stains confirm divergent differentiation  with cytokeratins being positive only in the epithelial areas and vimentin and desmin only in the sarcomatous regions  S 100 only stains the carcinoma  Although the differential diagnosis includes a metaplastic carcinoma with extensive sarcomatous areas  there is usually more blending of the epithelial and mesenchymal areas in metaplastic carcinoma  Also  immunoperoxidase usually shows some keratin positivity in the sarcomatous areas in a metaplastic carcinoma  Another interesting feature in this case is that the background of this tumor is reminiscent of a phylloides tumor  with broad stromal fronds focally covered by malignant epithelium  This feature raises the possibility that this tumor is arising in a high grade phylloides  All margins are greater than 0 2cm  No angiolymphatic invasion is seen  Dr  Koerner has reviewed the case and agrees with this interpretation  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 13 15                                                                                     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     ADDENDUM  ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION   The tumor size is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm  see gross description   No lymph nodes were identified in the axillary tail  Sectio