 of invasive carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0 1cm from the inked margin of the specimen along a broad front  Stains for receptors  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  A stain for E cadherin shows lack of membranous staining of the tumor cells  confirming the diagnoses of invasive lobular carcinoma and lobular neoplasia  lobular carcinoma in situ   GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm portion of breast tissue  oriented as follows  Short stitch anterior  long stitch lateral  bow tie cephalad  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  and inferior yellow  The specimen serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm firm  irregular  tan white mass that abuts the posterior margin  and comes to 1 1cm of the superior margin  1 3cm of the anterior margin  2 0cm from the inferior margin  1 5cm from the medial margin and 1 5cm from the lateral margin  The mass is encircled by dense white rubbery fibrotic tissue  The remainder of the breast contains focal rubbery fibrotic areas admixed with fat  the latter of which predominate  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to closest margins  superior and posterior    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Further representative sections of mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of more fibrotic appearing area adjacent to mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrosis away from mass  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm unoriented portion of breast tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm ellipse of tan skin on one surface  Also received in the same container are two irregular fragments of detached fatty tissue  aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMO