Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 34 CLINICAL DATA  75 year old female  status post right modified radical mastectomy for intraductal breast carcinoma ten years ago  now with a new left intraductal breast carcinoma for left modified radical mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION     INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  APOCRINE TYPE  MICROSCOPIC FOCUS     PREVIOUS BIOPSY CAVITY WITH DENSE FIBROSIS  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELLS  FAT NECROSIS  HEMOSIDERIN AND SKIN WITH SCAR     THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWENTY SEVEN OF TWENTY SEVEN LYMPH NODES  NOTE  The margins are free of carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 58                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received fresh labeled  Left breast   is a 27 x 19 x 5cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 25 x 13cm overlying skin ellipse  The skin contains a 1 0cm diameter unremarkable nipple and a 3 5cm diameter unremarkable areola  The skin is dark brown  12cm lateral to the nipple is a 3 0cm vertical  well healed surgical incision which is present 3 0cm from the lateral skin resection margin  and 1 5cm from the inferior and superior skin resection margins  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm  yellow to white  stellate area beneath the previously described incision site  The firm  gritty  stellate mass extends to within 0 4cm of the deep resection margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is soft  yellow to white  and unremarkable  The axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  and multiple REMOVED_DATE to 0 5cm soft  pink lymph nodes are dissected from it  SECTION CODE  A E  axillary tail lymph nodes  F J  entirety of deep margin of previous biopsy site  stellate mass  K M  representative sections of stellate mass previous biopsy cavity from medial to lateral  no margins   N  representative section of skin with scar  O  representative section of nipple  P  representative section of upper inner quadrant  at least 20cm from previous biopsy cavity  Q  representative section of lower inner quadrant  at least 20cm from previous biopsy cavity  R  representative section of lateral upper quadrant  at least 5cm from previous biopsy cavity  S T  additional axillary lymph nodes  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Not_assessed.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 46 CLINICAL DATA  Suture at short superior  long lateral                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY    INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  40    EXTENDING TO WITHIN LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED MARGIN  SLIDE D     DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  WITH COMEDO TYPE NECROSIS  60   EXTENDING TO AN INKED MARGIN  SLIDE I     ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA    FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Overall  the tumor is approximately 2 0cm in greatest dimension and the infiltrating component is 1 1cm in greatest dimension  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends into the breast parenchyma at a distance from the infiltrating component  No lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 41 Consulting Pathologist s   Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                      HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Negative  progesterone receptor  Negative  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 57     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 26     DNA FLOW CYTOMETRY Addendum     DNA FLOW CYTOMETRY  BREAST   DNA DIPLOID  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The coefficients of variation of the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  peaks for two blocks are REMOVED_DATE and 6 9   The calculated  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  phase fractions are REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE  S phase fractions  REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  M fractions  REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE Added by  Thomas J  Flotte  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing two sutures  the short one designating the superior  and the long one designating the lateral edge  The superior portion is inked yellow  Sectioning reveals a 1 1cm in diameter irregular firm nodule with stellate tan yellow mottled appearance  0 1cm from the nearest inked margin and 0 5cm from the lateral edge  The remaining parenchyma is tan yellow  rubbery  and focally hemorrhagic  Representative section of the firm area near the lateral edge is frozen as FX 1  The block is saved frozen  Representative tissue saved for ER studies  The remaining non frozen portion is submitted entirely in A through M  lateral to medial  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT BIOPSY   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
