ts of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 AUG 97 at 08 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number in four portions  Labeled  right breast tissue  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm breast with a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm skin ellipse  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 stellate gritty lesion with focal fibrous extension to the superior margin  Representative section of the superior margin is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in A  Three additional representative sections of the lesion are submitted in B D  The tissue away from the lesion is submitted in E G  Labeled  right breast  new deep margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked entirely  representative sections are submitted in H J  The cut surface of the specimen is unremarkable  Labeled  new superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm breast tissue with staple at old margin  The new superior margin is inked  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal no grossly obvious lesion at the new margin  Representative sections are submitted in K M  Labeled  axillary nodes  right  is an aggregate of fatty tissue with lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The lymph nodes are dissected  and representative sections are submitted in N R  Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST   SUPERIOR MARGIN  TUMOR EXTENDING CLOSE TO SUPERIOR MARGIN  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                           