Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 32 CLINICAL DATA  None                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   3 1 CM   POORLY DIFFERENTIATIED  NUCLEAR GRADE REMOVED_DATE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  No tumor is present at the resection margins  Tumor is present in lymphatic spaces  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   TWENTY FIVE OF TWENTY FIVE LYMPH NODES ARE NEGATIVE FOR METASTASES  Diagnosis by  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 11 Consulting Pathologist s   Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                      S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   1   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 56     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Negative  too low  progesterone receptor  Negative  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 25     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 08 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab is a 24 x 17 x 7cm modified mastectomy specimen with an attached 20 x 6cm skin ellipse including a 3cm unremarkable light tan nipple  There is also an attached 5 x 4 x 3cm axillary tail  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm ill defined light tan firm mass present 1 3cm from the inferior superficial margin  5cm inferior from the nipple  There is an additional REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm light tan irregular fibrotic area within the center of the specimen  A representative section of the tumor is frozen as FX 1 and saved for estrogen receptor studies  SECTION CODE  A  Inferior superficial margin  B  Nipple  C F  Sections of tumor  G  Section of fibrotic tissue  H L  Lymph nodes  Resident  Horace C  Wu  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST RIGHT   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
