Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 09 48 CLINICAL DATA  Ductal carcinoma in situ and lobular carcinoma in situ on right breast biopsy in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Lobular carcinoma in situ on the right in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   now for mastectomy on the right and prophylactic mastectomy on the left                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  SINGLE FOCUS SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPE  SINGLE FOCUS IN THE REGION OF THE BIOPSY CAVITY  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SINGLE FOCUS ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  COLLAGENOUS SPHERULOSIS  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 00                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two parts  Labeled  left breast   is a 210 gm mastectomy specimen  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm with long suture designating lateral and short suture designating superior  On the surface is a skin ellipse  REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm with a 3 5cm nipple and areola complex  No incision or lesions are noted  The external surface of the breast tissue is lobulated  fibroadipose tissue with fascia posteriorly  The breast tissue extends superiorly from the edge of the skin ellipse 10 0cm and inferiorly 2 3cm  The external surface is inked and the specimen is sectioned to reveal areas of white tan  soft  rubbery breast tissue throughout the specimen  No stellate areas are noted  Several cysts up to 0 2cm in diameter filled with clear fluid are present throughout the breast tissue  A representative section of the nipple and areola complex is submitted in cassette A  and representative sections of breast tissue are submitted in cassettes B through J  Labeled  right breast   is a 230 gm mastectomy specimen  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 2cm with long suture designating lateral and short suture designating superior  On the surface is a skin ellipse  REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm with eccentrically placed 3 5cm nipple and areola complex  2 5cm from the lateral edge of the nipple areola complex is a healing 2 2cm curvilinear scar extending 2 0cm from the lateral skin edge and to within 0 3cm of the superior margin  The breast tissue externally is lobulated  fibroadipose tissue with fascia in the posterior surface  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an area of yellow  gritty material with focal hemorrhage  1 1cm in greatest dimension extending to within 0 4cm of the deep margin and 1 1cm from the superior margin  The remaining breast tissue is white pink with focal cysts  No stellate lesions are identified  Representative sections from the biopsy cavity are submitted in cassettes K through O  representative section of the nipple and areola complex is submitted in cassette P and representative breast tissue with cysts in Q through T  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Taraneh Azar  M D  G  Gregory Gallico III  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Not_assessed.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  BISSON Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Kristina Braaten  M D  Reports To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Outside Material Received CLINICAL DATA  Tissue banking  Probable positive lymph nodes  Biopsy cavity is opened  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  MINUTE FOCI OF SMALL CELL CARCINOMA WITHIN THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE   TWENTY ADDITIONAL LYMPH NODES WITH NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  NOTE  Scattered minute foci of carcinoma are present within the reactive soft tissue of the prior sentinal lymph node biopsy site  The foci are visible on routine stains  with the largest focus spanning 0 04cm  micrometastasis   An immunohistochemical stain for keratin confirms the presence of carcinoma cells  Like the prior core biopsy   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    the tumor shows histologic features consistent with small cell carcinoma  This impression is supported by positivity for synaptophysin and chromogranin by immunohistochemistry  Small cell carcinoma occurs rarely in the breast  it cannot be differentiated from a metastasis from another site based on the histologic features  Clinical correlation is advised  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  MINUTE FOCUS OF SMALL CELL CARCINOMA WITHIN THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE  ALL RESECTION MARGINS NEGATIVE  SURGICAL CLEARANCE  REMOVED_DATE CM  INFERIOR MARGIN   SCLEROSING ADENOSIS HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of tan red fibroadipose tissue which is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm area which is sectioned to reveal a hemorrhagic cavity consistent with previous lymph node biopsy  The area shows yellow orange foci consistent with fat necrosis  Also noted are several tan pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 8cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Seven lymph nodes  in toto    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes  in toto    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes  in toto    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes  in toto    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest lymph node  bisected    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Hemorrhagic cavity  representative   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm yellow pink to white ovoid fibrofatty tissue  with a short stitch designating anterior  a long stitch designating lateral  and a bowtie designating cephalad  On the inferior and posterior aspects of the specimen  there are defects  communicating to a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm cavity  with a pink red hemorrhagic lining  The cavity also comes to within 0 1cm of the anterior margin  0 3cm to the lateral margin  and  1 5cm to the remaining two margins  The tissue surrounding the cavity varies from white and fibrotic to tan yellow and hemorrhagic  The remainder of the cut surface is yellow white and unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  superior green  inferior yellow  anterior blue  and posterior black  The specimen is submitted sequentially as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity to anterior aspect   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity to inferior defect   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity to include area to posterior defect  Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Michael R Tan  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  Selected outside slides of the patient s prior right breast excision were reviewed  Newton Wellesley Hospital   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    These show an invasive poorly differentiated carcinoma with focal areas of ductal differentiation  adjacent ductal carcinoma in situ  extensive lymphatic invasion  and a positive sentinel lymph node  macrometastasis   These findings confirm the breast origin of the tumor identified in the current specimen  The majority of the tumor shows morphologic features of neuroendocrine differentiation  namely  solid nests of cells with high nuclear grade  finely granular chromatin without nucleoli  nuclear molding  high mitotic index   50 10 HPF   karyorrhectic debris  areas of spindling  and abundant necrosis  Together with the strongly positive chromogranin stain in the current material  the tumor is classified as invasive ductal carcinoma with large component of high grade neuroendocrine differentiated carcinoma  Addendum by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , Poor_(grade_III).
