UCTAL HYPERPLASIA 2  RADIAL SCAR 3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA 4  HEALING BIOPSY SITE TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm  gross and microscopic measurement   GRADE  3  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Present BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Positive along a broad front at the superior margin of the specimen  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  NOTE  Sections of the right breast excision  part B  reveal invasive carcinoma growing in broad trabeculae and small nests of tumor cells with large geographic zones of keratinaceous necrosis and desmoplasia  The tumor cells are large with abundant dense keratinizing cytoplasm and have large central hyperchromatic nuclei with marked contour irregularities  vesicular chromatin and prominent macronucleoli  There is no tubule formation  Numerous mitotic figures  including atypical mitoses  are present  The morphologic findings are those of a high grade invasive ductal carcinoma with prominent squamous differentiation  also known as a metaplastic carcinoma  The extensive keratinization and cytomorphology are compatible with the large cell keratinizing variant of metaplastic carcinoma  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm soft tissue fragment  The adipose tissue is dissected to reveal 3 lymph nodes  Lymph node  1 is 1cm in greatest dimension and is not inked  Lymph node  2 is 0 9cm in greatest dimension and is inked blue  Lymph node  3 is 0 8cm in greatest dimension and is inked black  All 3 lymph nodes are bisected and submitted entirely as FX  1  now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 6cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  with a needle localization wire  There is a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The long axis of the specimen runs from anterior to posterior  The superior margin of the specimen is inked blue  the inferior black  the medial margin green  and the lateral margin yellow  It contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm ill defined  indurated  gray white mass  which extends to within 0 1cm of the superior  0 3cm of the inferior  0 6cm of the lateral  0 5cm of the medial  0 6cm of the anterior  and  2cm of the posterior  No clip is identified  The surrounding tissue is tan yellow to gray white and fibrofatty  The following representative sections are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior end  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior end  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of mass to nearest margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section away from mass  Received are 5 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  anterior margin  right breast   is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fragment of tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch in 1 surface designating the new margin  The surface containing the stitch is inked black  specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled with  posterior margin  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0 5cm fragment of tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on 1 surface designating the new margin  The surface containing the stitch is inked black  specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled with  medial margin  right breast   is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the new margin  The surface containing the stitch is inked black  specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_A