Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Resident  Christopher K Hysell  M D  Signed Out by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma of left breast with complete radiologic response following neoadjuvant chemotherapy FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH CHEMOTHERAPY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  FIBROTIC BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  see gross description  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received unfixed  labeled  Pauline Wright  REMOVED_DATE  left breast lumpectomy  is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast tissue  The surgeon orients the lateral margin with a long suture and the superior margin with a short suture  The long axis of the specimen runs in the lateral to medial plane  The specimen is inked as follows  posterior black  anterior blue  superior green  and inferior yellow  A localization wire identifies a clip in the lateral portion of the specimen  The tissue is fibrous with scattered areas consistent with fibrocystic change  The specimen is entirely submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   En face medial resection margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   En face lateral resection margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Serial sectioning from lateral to medial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative section from the medial aspect of the specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remaining tissue such that the specimen is entirely submitted  Fellow Review by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13 25 CLINICAL DATA  Recurrent breast cancer  stitch 12 o clock                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  RECURRENT INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3 OF 3  WITHIN SKIN AND SUBAREOLAR TISSUE  SEE NOTE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3 OF 3  WITHIN AND BEYOND THE REGION OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Lymphatic invasion is noted in the dermis and subareolar region  All resection margins are negative for carcinoma  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 17 10                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block A   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 16 19     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     NOTE  This case is re examined at the request of Dr  Irene Kuter to establish the dimensions of the invasive component  The invasive tumor is present on 2 of 7 sections and is REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm as measured from slide A  It mostly involves the dermis of the nipple  The presence of ductal carcinoma in situ adjacent to the invasive component raises the possibility that this is a new primary tumor rather than a true recurrence  although the latter possibilty cannot be excluded  Lymphatic invasion is identified  but it is not extensive  Added by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 02 at 16 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm right simple mastectomy specimen  with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 4cm tan skin ellipse  There is an eccentric 2 3cm areola with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm firm  flattened  tan red nipple  There is a 2 3cm scar arising 0 4cm superolateral to the nipple  A black stitch designates the 12 o clock aspect  The resection margin is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 9 x 3 7cm region of dense gray white fibrosis with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm region of diffuse hemorrhage deep to the nipple which comes to 1 0cm of the superficial margin and 2 5cm of the deep margin  The remaining cut surface is 70  tan yellow lobular and 30  gray white fibrous tissue  No lymph nodes are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Hemorrhagic focus to nipple and deep margin B  Skin to hemorrhagic focus and superficial and deep margins C D  Hemorrhagic focus with surrounding fibrous tissue and skin E  Deep margin to hemorrhagic focus F G  Representative dense fibrous tissue away from hemorrhagic focus Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  LAN WANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Poor_(grade_III).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 49 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA  THREE MICROSCOPIC FOCI  0 1  REMOVED_DATE  AND REMOVED_DATE CM   PRESENT IN THE WALL OF THE BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE   RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FOCALLY INVOLVING SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  AND FOCALLY PRESENT AT THE ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   Note  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The area of ductal carcinoma in situ that is present at the anterior margin is less than 0 1cm in total size  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 23 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 35                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Lymph Node  Left Axilla   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are two specimens  Labeled  left breast  short superior  long lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm skin ellipse excised a depth of 0 3cm and containing a 2 5cm well healed linear scar  There is a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  a short stitch designating the superior aspect and a double stitch designating the inferior   deep   margin  The anterior aspect is inked in blue while the posterior is inked in black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity with a hemorrhagic  fibrous tract extending to the skin ellipse  There is a firm  tan white  hemorrhagic nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm present in the posterior wall of the biopsy cavity  The cavity is 0 6cm from the posterior inferior margin and 0 6cm from the anterior margin  The rim of stellate fibrosis extends to the posterosuperior and posteroinferior margins  Apparently contiguous with the nodule in the biopsy cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm well circumscribed soft tissue mass with a tan yellow  hemorrhagic rim and brown  variegated center  This nodule is present at the anterior margin and 0 5cm from the posterior margin  Representative sections are taken lateral to medial as follows  SECTION CODE A  Biopsy cavity  nearest  posterior  margin  B  Inferior biopsy cavity  C D  Superior aspect biopsy cavity  E  Fibrous tract to skin from biopsy cavity  F  Inferior aspect biopsy cavity  G  Superior aspect biopsy cavity  H  Hemorrhagic nodule  closest margin anterior  I J  Fibrous areas  Labeled as  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of adipose tissue from which multiple lymph nodes are extracted ranging in size from 0 2cm to 1 2cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes have been submitted in cassettes K through R  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
