ass grossly extends to less than 0 2cm from the superficial margin  2 0cm from the inferior resection margin  0 5cm from the deep resection margin  0 5cm from the closest lateral margin and 1 5cm from the closest medial resection margin  Representative section of this Representative sections of breast showing fibrous areas in G H  Additional reprsentative sections suspicious for invasive and in situ carcinoma in GG II  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in 5 parts  Labelled  additional superficial margin  are multiple fragments of unoriented focally yellow and focally white fibrous breast tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  Representative sections submitted in cassettes I K   Additional medial margins right breast  are multiple fragments of unoriented soft yellow breast tissue in aggregate of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  representative sections submitted in cassettes L N  Labelled  final shave margin right breast  are multiple fragments of soft yellow oriented breast tissue in aggregate of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  representative sections in cassettes O W   approximately REMOVED_DATE of the specimen are submitted for histologic examination   Labelled  right axillary contents  is an aggregate of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm The specimen is sectioned to reveal multiple lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 3 5cm in greatest diameter  The largest two lymph nodes are sectioned to reveal gray tan homogenous cut surface  suspicious for metastatic disease  One half of each of these 2 suspicious lymph nodes in cassettes X Y  and the remaining lymph nodes in cassettes Z DD  Labelled  additional axillary tissue  are multiple fragments of fibrofatty tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The specimen is sectioned to reveal 3 lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm  the largest lymph node is bisected and submitted in cassette EE and the remaining lymph nodes in FF  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1  SUPERFICIAL MEDIAL MARGIN  GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  PROBABLY NON INVASIVE  O R  Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  ADDITIONAL   EXCISION PART D  SOFT TISSUE  RIGHT BREAST   ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL PART E  SOFT TISSUE  RIGHT BREAST   ADDITIONAL MEDIAL MARG PART F  SOFT TISSUE  RIGHT BREAST   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
