ared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 10 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm tan and firm lymph node with attached tan yellow fat  The fat is trimmed and the lymph node is bivalved to reveal a homogenous tan white firm area  suspicious for metastasis  Half of the lymph node is frozen as FX 1  resubmitted in cassette A  The remaining half of the lymph node is submitted entirely in cassette B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm right modified radical mastectomy specimen with a long suture designating the axillary tail and a short suture designating 12 o clock  The deep resection margin is black inked  the superior is blue inked  Present in the anterior portion of the mastectomy specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm nipple areolar complex  The skin of the nipple is tan and unremarkable  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm tan rubbery firm area  which comes to 1 5cm to the deep margin  black   5 0cm to the inferior margin and 3 0cm to the nipple  anterior   Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section code  C D  rubbery firm area to deep  black  margin  radial  E H  representative sections of rubbery firm area  I J  representative sections of unremarkable breast parenchyma away from rubbery firm area  Attached to the mastectomy specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm area of axillary tail  The lymph nodes are dissected and submitted entirely as follows  Section code  K M  all lymph nodes  whole  Received fresh   labeled REMO