a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node and associated fat  bivalved and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast re excision   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm oriented breast tissue  with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  There is a 2 5cm linear defect on the anterior surface  exposing the biopsy cavity  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior  black  superior green and inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm biopsy cavity  lined by tan pink granular tissue and surrounded by punctate yellow areas  grossly consistent with fat necrosis  The biopsy cavity is 0 3cm from inferior  superior  and posterior margin and 0 6cm from the anterior margin  1 2cm from the lateral margin and 1 6cm from medial margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm white fibrous area  anterior to the biopsy cavity and abutting the anterior margin  approximately 1 4cm from the lateral margin  There is also REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm white fibrous area  0 8cm from the medial margin  abutting the anterior margin  Residual tumor is not grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity  closest superior and posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity  closest inferior margin and fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity  closest anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity and surrounding fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections away from the biopsy cavity  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional medial margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm oriented breast tissue with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating new medial margin  The new medial margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal the edge of the biopsy cavity  0 4cm from the new medial margin with focal fat necrosis  The specimen is entirely submitted from superior to inferior in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Nicole Ann Belsley M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Nicole Ann Belsley M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL   665  311   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION , Moderate_(grade_II).
