asuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm  The anterior surface is inked blue and the posterior surface is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal dense  white fibrous tissue throughout  There is a scarred region measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm located in the medial half of the breast  It is 0 5cm from the posterior margin and 0 9cm from the anterior margin  The lesion lies 2 2cm deep and superior to the medial aspect of the nipple  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Scarred area to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Scarred region to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Scarred region to overlying skin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Scarred area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Scarred area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous tissue away from scarred area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fatty tissue with possible lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of yellow red fatty tissue containing multiple lymph nodes  The fat is dissected away to reveal multiple lymph nodes  the largest of which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three potential nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four potential nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three potential nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four potential nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  port a cath is a silver circular catheter port and a length of blue tubing measuring 25cm  Specimen is for gross examination only  Gross Dictation by Miriam D Post M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Miriam D Post M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 Additional diagnostic information  The ductal carcinoma in situ is present in 6 of 8 representative blocks of breast parenchyma  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  2 by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION PART C  HARDWARE  PORT A  CATH   REMOVAL , Poor_(grade_III).
