Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 27 CLINICAL DATA  44 year old woman with advanced breast tissue damage and fungating infection                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATIN DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  WITH METAPLASTIC CHONDROID COMPONENT  METAPLASTIC CARCINOMA   13 CM  PRESENT AT DEEP SURGICAL RESECTION MARGIN AND ULCERATING THROUGH OVERLYING SKIN  SEE NOTE  2  LYMPH NODES  5  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  NOTE  Tumor abuts the area designated by the surgeon as  nipple remnant   No lymphatic or vascular space invasion is seen  Dr  Koerner has reviewed all slides and agrees  Diagnosis by  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 18 53 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT  BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   13   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 57     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Negative  progesterone receptor  Negative  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 27     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 08 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a 4 x 2 x 1cm piece of firm  white yellow breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal firm  white tissue and yellow fat  Representative section is frozen as FX 1 and kept frozen  The remainder is submitted entirely in A and B  Received fresh later  is a  REMOVED_CASE_ID  gram  partial mastectomy specimen consisting of 15 x 12cm black skin with underlying 21 x 14 x 11cm firm  white yellow tissue and attached 7 x 4 x 3cm piece of axillary adipose tissue  Two sutures are present on the skin  The longer one designates lateral and the short one designates the superior margin  The external surface of the skin is remarkable for a 15 x 11cm bulging white yellow  friable mass with a 6 x 2cm central ulceration which is 4cm deep within the breast parenchyma  The mass is within less than 0 5cm of the lateral skin resection margins  at multiple foci both superiorly and inferiorly  2cm from the lateral axillary skin resection margin and 2 5cm from the medial skin resection margin  The nipple is not identifiable but a pin is present designated by the surgeon as nipple remnant  Further sectioning reveals entire involvement of the breast by firm  white yellow  focally friable tissue  The mass measures 11 x 6 x 13cm beneath the skin and extends to the inked deep soft tissue margins as well as superior inferior soft tissue margins  Also present is REMOVED_DATE x 4 x 4cm piece of red tan skeletal muscle superiorly adjacent to the axillary adipose tissue  The mass appears to infiltrate the skeletal muscle in a nodular fashion  The axillary adipose tissue contains several lymph nodes with white tan  solid cut surfaces  the largest 1 2cm in greatest diameter  Section Code  C  skin ends from both lateral and medial resection margins  D  inked deep soft tissue margins  E  tumor and skin from superior edge  F  tumor and skin from inferior edge  G  nipple remnant and representative junction of skin with tumor  H J  more representative tumor  K  lymph nodes  L  representative skeletal muscle  M  designated nipple remnant  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST RIGHT BIOPSY   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Debra F Weinstein  M D  Kimberly S Kirkwood  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 MAY 03 ACCESSIONED ON  02 MAY 03 at 11 32 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  FOCAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 1  ADJACENT TO LATERAL BIOPSY SITE AND FAR AWAY FROM RESECTION MARGINS  2  FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  SECOND BIOPSY SITE IN SUPERIOR LOCATION  4  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 22 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  08 MAY 03 at 17 25                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast with REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm of attached axillary tissue  The overlying tan REMOVED_DATE x 10 3cm skin has an eccentrically located REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm unremarkable everted nipple  There are 2 well healed linear scars 4 0cm apart  The first  3 5cm superior to the nipple  measures 5 0cm in length  the other  5 2cm lateral to the nipple  measures 3 0cm in length  The specimen is inked blue along the anterior and black along the posterior  Contiguous with the superior scar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm gray white  firm  stellate area consistent with a biopsy site  which comes to 1 5cm of the posterior and 2 0cm of the anterior margin  Located 5 0cm lateral and inferior to this cavity  contiguous with the second  lateral  scar is an additional REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm tan gray  firm stellate area consistent with a biopsy site  which comes to 2 0cm of the anterior and 2 8cm of the posterior margins  The remaining cut surface consists of unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue  Within the axillary fat  multiple tan  rubbery lymph nodes ranging from 0 3cm to 2 0cm are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODES  A C  superior cavity  D   posterior margin closest to superior cavity  E   anterior margin closest to superior cavity  F H  lateral cavity  I   anterior margin closest to lateral cavity  J   posterior margin closest to lateral cavity  K   parenchyma between both cavities  L M  parenchyma away from both cavities  N Q  whole lymph nodes  multiple per cassette  R   one lymph node bisected  S T  one lymph node sectioned  Gross Description by  CHRISTINE D AMATO Resident  ELENA BRACHTEL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Well_differentiated_(grade_I).
