Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 21 CLINICAL DATA  Mass of right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE ADENOCARCINOMA REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 1  MUCINOUS TYPE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor extends 0 1cm from the superior margin both anteriorly and deep  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  BREAST  RIGHT NEW DEEP MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT NEW SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT NEW MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT NEW INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT NEW LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 39                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 35 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  new deep margin  suture on true margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue  with a suture on one aspect  The sutured margin is inked blue  the remainder of the specimen is inked black  The suture designated the true margin on the new deep margin  Sectioning reveals unremarkable parenchyma  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  new superior margin  suture on true margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of white yellow fibroadipose tissue with a suture on one aspect designating the new true margin on the superior aspect  The sutured margin is inked blue  the remainder of the specimen is inked black  Sectioning reveals white fibrous parenchyma with no discrete lesions  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette C D  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  new medial margin  suture on true margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm white yellow portion of breast tissue  with a suture on one aspect designating the true margin of the new medial margin  The sutured aspect is inked blue  the remainder of the specimen is inked black  Sectioning reveals no discrete lesions and the specimen is entirely submitted in cassette E  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  new inferior margin  suture on true margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm portion of yellow breast tissue with a suture on one aspect designating the true new inferior margin  The sutured aspect is inked blue  the remainder is inked black  Sectioning reveals no discrete lesions  and the specimen is entirely submitted in cassette F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  new lateral margin  suture on true margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE portion of yellow breast tissue with a suture on one aspect designating the true new lateral margin  The sutured aspect is inked blue  the remainder black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal no discrete lesions and is entirely submitted in cassette G  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right lumpectomy  stitch lateral  short stitch superior  very long stitch deep margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm oriented right lumpectomy specimen with a localizing wire extending from superior to inferior in the midportion of the specimen  There is a short suture designating the superior aspect which is inked yellow  a long suture designates the lateral margin  which is inked blue  A very long suture designates the deep margin  inked black  The superior is inked red  the medial green  and the inferior orange  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm well delineated white  focally red firm nodule which focally abuts the anterolateral margin as well as the medial margin  The tumor comes within 0 5cm of the closest deep margin  0 9cm from the closest superior margin  and 2 0cm from the inferior margin  The parenchyma surrounding the lesion is composed predominantly of unremarkable fat  There is a collection of dense fibrous tissue along the deep margin  The mass is entirely submitted from superior to inferior in cassettes H J  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDA