Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 MAY 01 ACCESSIONED ON  09 MAY 01 at 11 36 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer  with positive margins on lumpectomy  4 01   done at MGH                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL TUMOR  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH FOCAL MODERATE DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  14 MAY 01 at 14 49                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  re excision  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm rectangular white yellow lobulated fibrofatty portion of breast oriented by a short suture designating the superior and a long suture designating the lateral margins on the anterior aspect  The specimen bares a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm unremarkable ellipse of skin with a 4 0cm well healed scar  The specimen is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm cavitary lesion centrally located  0 2cm of the superior margin and the anterior aspect underlying the skin ellipse  The specimen is inked as follows  superior   black and inferior   blue  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm cavity that extends along the long axis of the specimen and is surrounded by fat necrosis and hemorrhage  The remainder of parenchyma is yellow and lobulated fibrofatty tissue and is devoid of any nodules or masses  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral  Section Code  A  Superior medial  B  Inferior medial and fat necrosis  C  Posterior with hemorrhagic foci  D  Inferior and hemorrhagic foci  E  Anterior with skin ellipse  F  Superior lateral  G  Posterior lateral  H  Infer