pect  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm biopsy cavity in the mid inferior portion of the specimen  The biopsy cavity is surrounded by tan yellow fibrotic tissue  and is 0 8cm from the deep resection margin  1 2cm from the anterior skin  and greater than 2 5cm from any other resection margins  Further sectioning reveals a 1 5cm tan necrotic nodule 3 0cm superior to the biopsy cavity and is greater than 2 0cm from all resection margins  The remaining parenchyma is predominantly yellow fatty with focal tan fibrotic areas  SECTION CODES  A D  Biopsy cavity with deep resection margin  E G  Additional sections of biopsy cavity  H  Representative sections of the smaller nodule  I  Representative uninvolved parenchyma  J M  Axillary lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right additional axillary node  is 1 tan firm nodule measuring 0 3cm in greatest dimension  entirely submitted in cassette N  Resident  QUN DONG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Gerald Sidney Foster  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY   EXCISION   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
