eared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 13 57 Proofread by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm breast lumpectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm skin ellipse  There are two localizing wires in the middle portion of the specimen  There is one stitch designating superior and two stitches designating medial  The specimen is entirely inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm white firm nodule between the two localizing wires in the blue colored parenchyma  The nodule is grossly approximately 0 7cm from the closest inferior margin  1 3cm from the closest superior margin  and 1 5cm from anterior skin  The remaining margins are at least 3 0cm away from the nodule  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A E  inferior half of the area around the nodule  from medial to lateral with the nodule in B and C  ink represents inferior margin   F K  superior half of the suspicious area  ink represents superior margin   L M  closest deep margin N  medial margin O  lateral margin Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left sentinel node  are two fragments of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The larger specimen contains a blue colored lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The specimen is entirely frozen as FX 1 now as P  Resident  LAN WANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  LE