egative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 53     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR C ERB  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PROTEIN AS REPORTED BY IMPATH BREAST  RIGHT   Five percent  5   of the tumor cells stain for c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   favorable   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast tissue  Inked as follows  lateral  long stitch  black  superior  short  green  inferior yellow  anterior red  posterior blue  and medial black  The specimen is sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal multiple hard  white tan  well circumscribed nodules abutting the red inked margin  Frozen section of one of the nodules is FX 1 and saved frozen to Cox 5  An additional piece of tissue is saved  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted in cassettes A through E  Lateral margin is in cassette A  Medial margin in cassette E  Labeled  right breast 7 o clock  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of breast tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm yellow tan well circumscribed mass  entirely submitted in cassette F and G  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                       