ntative section of a granular area is frozen as FX 1  now submitted in cassette A  A representative section of the papillomas is submitted in cassette B  Representative sections of fibrous and granular breast tissue with association to the deep posterior margin are submitted in cassettes C J  from medial to lateral  The axillary tissue is examined for lymph nodes  and there are six lymph nodes which are submitted in cassette K  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left MRM   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axilla  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 7 5cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable 1 0cm everted nipple  The posterior aspect of the specimen is inked in black  and serially sectioned to reveal an ill defined  gritty  tan white area of firm and fibrous breast parenchyma which measures approximately 5 0cm in greatest dimension and is located 0 5cm from deep margin  and more than 4 0cm from superior  more than 6 0cm from inferior  more than 5 0cm from medial  and more than 13cm from lateral margins  There is a separate stellate lesion with tan white color and a chalky punctate surface  which measures approximately 1 5cm in diameter and is located 1 0cm from deep margin  the closest margin   Inferiorly  there is an additional tan yellow firm well circumscribed lobulated nodule  measuring 0 7cm in diameter  located 0 7cm from deep margin  The rest of the specimen is grossly unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  The axillary tail is examined for lymph nodes  L Q  Ill defined mass with deep resection margin  R S  Stellate lesion  T  Inferior lobulated nodule  U  Parenchyma  V X  Whole lymph nodes  Resident  ALIREZA SEPEHR  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  NORMA RODRIGUEZ  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                               