nicates with the medial and posterior margin  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior margin is inked blue  the superior margin is inked green  and the inferior margin is inked yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned medial to lateral to reveal diffuse dense gray white fibrous tissue which hemorrhage and chalky yellow discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  No discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities are identified  The specimen is entirely submitted  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the medial end margin radially sectioned as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the lateral end margin radially sectioned as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margin  lateral half of cavity   are two irregular portions of gray white to tan yellow fibrofatty tissue with no orientation  which measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Sectioning reveals dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesion or other gross abnormality  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast  final margin  medial half of cavity   are four irregular portions of gray white to tan pink fibrofatty tissue which aggregate to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Sectioning reveals dense gray white fibrous tissue  and the specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Breast  Left   Reexcision PART B  Breast  Left  Final Margin  Lateral Half of Cavity   Excision PART C  Breast  Left  Final Margin  Medial Half of Cavity   Excision  report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
