eceived fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axilla  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm portion of adipose tissue which contains multiple tan red rubbery lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 6cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  G  3 whole lymph nodes H  2 lymph nodes I  3 whole lymph nodes J  3 whole lymph nodes K O  1 bisected lymph node in each  Gross Description by  LORI MARINI Resident  ANUPAMA GUPTA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION   report_end  , Moderate_(grade_II).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 18 47 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen is free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN ONE OF FOURTEEN LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The metastatic focus spans less than 0 2cm and is confined to the lymph node  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 42                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 AUG 96 at 08 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right modified radical mastectomy  is a right breast measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm with an overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm with a 3 x 3cm areola and nipple and an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail  A REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm ill defined white  hard mass located centrally in the tissue is identified  The mass is located 1 0cm below the skin and 0 4cm from the deepest resection margin which is the closest resection margin  The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable  The largest axillary lymph node measures 2 0cm in diameter and is firm and pin  SECTION CODE A  Tumor and closest margin  deep   B F  Tumor mass closest margin  deep   G L  Lymph nodes  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Janey Pratt  M D  Armaghan A Mostafavi  M D  PART   BREAST  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Moderate_(grade_II).
