orrhage  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One end  en face    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue at tip of first localization wire   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of first cavity to margin with tissue adjacent to second localization wire tip as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue between cavities   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Second cavity to margin with area of metal clip as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and tissue adjacent to tip of localization wire as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Alternate end  en face   Received are seven additional containers which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Kreusser  REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast cephalad   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm portion of gray white to tan yellow fibrofatty tissue with no orientation  Sectioning reveals dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast biopsy medial   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm portion of gray white to tan yellow fibrofatty tissue with no orientation  Sectioning reveals focally dense gray pink fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast biopsy  posterior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm unoriented portion of unremarkable  focally hemorrhagic tan yellow fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast biopsy  caudad   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm unoriented portion of unremarkable  focally hemorrhagic tan yellow fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast biopsy  lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOV