Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 MAY 04 ACCESSIONED ON  11 MAY 04 at 13 09 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma  status post chemotherapy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH FEATURES OF CHEMOTHERAPY EFFECT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH FEATURES OF CHEMOTHERAPY EFFECT  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SCLEROSING ADENOSIS WITH CALCIFICATIONS  PROFIFERATIVE FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  0 1 CM DEPOSIT  WITH FOCAL EXTRANODAL EXTENSION IN 1 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  Multiple scattered microscopic foci up to 1 CM  Grade  cannot assess due to superimposed chemotherapy effect  Lymphatic vessel invasion  absent  Blood vessel invasion  absent  Margin of invasive carcinoma  more than REMOVED_DATE CM from margins  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  within and beyond region of region of invasive tumor  Grade of ductal carcinoma in situ  cannot assess due to chemotherapy effect  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  more than REMOVED_DATE CM from margins  Stains for receptors  performed on prior specimens  Note  Careful gross evaluation of the axillary tail revealed multiple potential lymph nodes which were all submitted for microscopic evaluation however all but 2  which were lymph nodes  represented dense fibrous nodular tissue  Submission of additional axillary tissue did not reveal additional lymph nodes  Diagnosis by  JOSEPH T  RABBAN  M D   M P H  Signed On  18 MAY 04 at 07 56                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm right breast with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The specimen is surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE tan pink skin ellipse  There is an eccentric REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm unremarkable tan areolar with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm unremarkable nipple  No apparent scars or other gross abnormalities are noted  A black stitch designates the 12 o clock aspect as per requisition  The anterior surface is inked blue  and the posterior is black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a diffusely gray white fibrous tissue with multiple enlarged  smooth walled cysts  Some of the cysts contain a gray tan grumous substance  The cyst walls are gray white and fibrous and average 0 1cm in thickness  The cysts come to 1 5cm of the posterior margin  and are diffusely distributed throughout the mammary tissue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm area of diffuse marked hemorrhage in the upper outer quadrant which comes to 4 0cm of the posterior margin  Within this hemorrhagic area is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm lesion consistent with biopsy  which comes to 5 0cm of the deep margin  No other lesions or other gross abnormalities are noted  Sectioning of the axillary tail reveals numerous tan pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 9cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted from lateral to medial as follows  A  Representative fibrous tissue to deep margin  B  Representative fibrous tissue including cysts to deep margin  C  Deep margin closest to hemorrhagic area  radial section   D F  Hemorrhagic area  with firm lesion  possibly representing previous biopsy site as D  G  Additional representative fibrous tissue including cysts  H  Multiple lymph nodes in toto  I J  Multiple lymph nodes in toto  K  One lymph node trisected  L O  Lymph node candidates  with one lymph node bisected as M  P Q  Representative upper outer quadrant  R S  Representative