Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  25 AUG 97 at 19 54 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INFERIOR MEDIAL RESECTION MARGIN   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE   SEE NOTE   3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  Note  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The margins appear free of ductal carcinoma in situ  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL  13  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  BREAST   RIGHT BREAST MASS  ADDITIONAL MARGIN  STITCH OR DEEPEST MARGIN    BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  28 AUG 97 at 16 00                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 10 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  oriented breast biopsy  which is inked as follows  medial half black  lateral blue  anterior green  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm white gritty firm nodule  within 0 15cm of the inferior margin  and 0 4cm of the deep resection margin  In the medial aspect of the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular  white  firm area  The remaining parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Section Code  A D  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm nodule in relationship to the closest margins  E H  representative sections of the irregular  white  firm area in relation to the margins I  representative unremarkable breast tissue from the lateral portion of the specimen J  representative uninvolved tissue from the medial portion of the specimen  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  additional margin  stitch on deepest margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink fatty adipose tissue with a suture  The entirely specimen is inked black  and the deep margin  designated by suture  is overlaid with green  The specimen is sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes K through O  Labeled  axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan red fatty adipose tissue  Lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in casettes P through T  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD                                                         