ED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm nipple  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial to lateral axis to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan pink to tan white  firm  ill defined and focally cystic mass which lies 0 2cm from the posterior  1 5cm from the inferior  5 0cm from the anterior  3 0cm from the superior  2 0cm from the lateral  and 5 0cm from the medial margins  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan white  ill defined firm area which lies 0 6cm medial and anterior to the first fairly well defined mass and lies 2 0cm from the posterior  2 5cm from the inferior  4 0cm from the superior  4 5cm from the anterior  3 0cm from the lateral  and 4 0cm from the medial margins  The rest of the breast parenchyma displays a tan yellow lobulated cut surface and contains a focal cluster of cystic spaces which extrude the tan brown pasty material on pressure  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire first tan pink irregular mass to include closest inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire thickened tan pink irregular mass to include closest inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Intervening nodular breast parenchyma between the first and second mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  focally cystic breast parenchyma away from mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   En face section  medial margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   En face section  lateral margin  Received are seven containers which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  uterus  cervix   is a 211 gram hysterectomy specimen which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm  The posterior cervical margin is inked black  and the anterior cervical margin is inked blue  Opening the specimen reveals a large REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 7cm solid tan white mass with an epicenter in the upper portion of the myometrium to involve both the anterior and posterior aspects of the myometrium  This mass causes a 5 7cm exophytic protrusion into the anterior and posterior endomyometrium  The mass is very homogeneous with an only 1 0cm greatest dimension area of hemorrhage and very rare areas which are darker yellow  0 1cm in greatest dimension   Overall the mass does not display areas of softening or necrosis  There is a distinct border between the mass and the normal appearing myometrium  The mass involves almost the entire width of the myometrium and depth wise comes to within 0 4cm of the serosa in places  The boundary of the mass with the overlying endometrium is blurred with a suggestion of a 0 1cm thick endometrium overlying the mass  The exophytic portion of this mass which protrudes the endometrial cavity is  3 0cm from both the anterior and posterior lower uterine segment  The endometrium distal to the mass shows focal roughening and appears to be  0 1cm in thickness  The myometrium in the uninvolved portion of the specimen is up to 1 1cm in thickness  The mucosa of the cervix displays a tan pink herringbone like appearance and is unremarkable  The serosa of the specimen is smooth  The following sections are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative full cross section of the mass with its relation to the endometrium  myometrium and serosa as diagrammed   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections displaying the relationship of the mass to the overlying endometrium   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of the mass including the area of hemorrhage and the darker speckled yellow areas   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Full thickness representative section of the posterior cervix   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative full thickness section from the posterior LUS   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Full thickness representative section from the anterior cervix   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Full thickness