Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 AUG 03 ACCESSIONED ON  12 AUG 03 at 15 46 CLINICAL DATA  Left axillary sentinel lymph node biopsy for staging  Poorly differentiated carcinoma with signet ring cells with focal lymphatic invasion  Left simple mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODES  LEFT SENTINEL   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Numerous scattered tumor cells  hundreds per lymph node  are identified in the subcapsular sinuses of both lymph nodes  on H E and confirmatory cytokeratin immunostains  Extranodal involvement is not seen  When evaluated in conjunction with the permanent sections  scattered tumor cells can be identified on the frozen section slides  However  in isolation  the frozen section findings are not felt to be definitive  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  PLEOMORPHIC TYPE  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE AND TABLE  1  NOTE  The signet ring cell morphology seen in the core biopsy is not as prominent now that the complete tumor is available for evaluation  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm Grade  3 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Present Blood vessel invasion  Not identified Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater Stains for receptors  Requested Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  15 AUG 03 at 15 52                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block G   Few tumor cells stain faintly for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain faintly for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression