thology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 11 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel lymph node  1   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fibroadipose breast tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node  The lymph node is frozen as fx  1  The specimen is submitted entirely in A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node  2  667  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm lymph node with an attached fibrous breast tissue entirely frozen as fx  2  The specimen is resubmitted in B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right lumpectomy of right breast   is a lumpectomy of fibrofatty breast tissue which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  The specimen is oriented by the surgeon with a double knot on the anterior surface  a short stitch superiorly  and a longer stitch medially  The anterior half is inked black  the posterior half is inked blue and the superior surface is red  The specimen is sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal an ill defined white  firm  gritty tumor that is located mainly in the medial half of the specimen and measures about 1 5cm in greatest dimension  The closest margin of the specimen to the tumor is inferior posterior  which measures 0 5cm  The rest of the parenchyma has fibrosis and microcysts  Representative sections are submitted as follows  C F  Entire tumor with inferior margin  G  Cyst close to tumor  H  Representative sections from parenchyma far from tumor  I  Parenchyma above the tumor with superior margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  subareolar lateral margin  is a fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in J K  Resident  BIZHAN BANDARCHI CHAMKHALEH  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   SENTINEL NODE  1  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2   SENTINEL NODE  2  667  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  Mari Mino  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  1 PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  2 PART C  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART D  BREAST  SUBAREOLAR  LATERAL   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Well_differentiated_(grade_I).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 53 CLINICAL DATA  Large lobular carcinoma with lobular carcinoma in situ on outside biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA FORMING SEVERAL SMALL NODULES BOTH ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY CAVITY AND AWAY FROM IT  IN SITU CARCINOMA  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 8 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The in situ carcinoma exhibits a mixture of ductal and lobular characteristics  The invasive carcinoma forms several seemingly discrete nodules  making the size of the infiltrating component impossible to determine  The largest focus measures 0 4cm  and together the foci probably aggregate to about 1 0cm  Blood vessl and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  The tumor in the axillary lymph node spans about 0 3cm in greatest dimension in tissue section  and the cells extend into axillary fat  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 52                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number only is an 805 gram modified radical mastectomy specimen  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm with an axillary tail REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and overlying skin ellipse REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm  At the central aspect of the inferior skin margin is a 2 5cm areola and nipple  and a healing scar is present 2 0cm in length extending to within 0 8cm to the superior margin and beginning 8 0cm from the medial margin of the skin ellipse  The specimen is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm biopsy cavity extending to within 0 7cm of the deep margin and to within 0 4cm of the superior margin  The remaining breast is unremarkable  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail  A 0 5cm  hard  well circumscribed nodule is identified 3 0cm deep to the nipple  Section code  A D  biopsy site with deep margin E  biopsy site with superior margin F J  representative breast tissue K  well circumscribed nodule L  nipple M O  axillary lymph nodes Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael L Grossbard  M D  PART   RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Well_differentiated_(grade_I).
