Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 AUG 01 ACCESSIONED ON  16 AUG 01 at 14 19 CLINICAL DATA  79 y o  lady with invasive right breast cancer on excisional biopsy from REMOVED_DATE                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 EXAMINED LYMPH NODE  NOTE  Keratin immunostains are negative for tumor cells  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3  SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  LOCATED FAR AWAY FROM MARGINS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  24 AUG 01 at 17 29                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a simple mastectomy specimen consisting of a right breast measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm and an overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm  The specimen is oriented with a long suture at the lateral margin  and a short suture at the superior margin  There is a healed linear scar measuring 4 0cm on the inferior aspect of the skin ellipse and an inverted nipple  The specimen is inked black  Beneath the scar  there is a biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  with fibrotic tissue surrounding it  The cavity is 0 8cm from the closest margin  which is the deep margin  and about 6 0cm to the next closet margins  Medial to the biopsy cavity is a firm nodular area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  and is 2 0cm from the closest margin  which is the deep margin  The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a lymph node containing blue dye  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  Also in the same container is a piece of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  SECTION CODES  A D  Biopsy cavity with fibrotic area around  with B containing cavity closest to the deep margin  E F  Nodular area medial to biopsy cavity  G H  Normal parenchyma  I   Skin with scar  J   Sentinel lymph node  bisected  K   Fatty tissue received with sentinel lymph node  L M  Biopsy cavity  N O  Nipple  Resident  SHABIN NANJI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Steven Michael Abbate  M D  David R Whittaker  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Well_differentiated_(grade_I).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 00 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 31                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm aggregate of soft  tan cores  submitted in toto in cassette A  Gross Description by  Joe Serra Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
